0..75 Comment "// Two seats share one binary session. Each seat draws one fair bit through"
76..151 Comment "// `std.rand.Eff` and sends it to the other seat. Each seat answers whether"
152..219 Comment "// the two bits agree, and `exchanged` answers the pair of answers."
220..222 Comment "//"
223..296 Comment "// A session between seats is one program, the choreography of its seats."
297..372 Comment "// Its draws happen in two tasks, and the exact model answers each draw. So"
373..450 Comment "// the pair has an exact distribution, though the two tasks run in turns that"
451..474 Comment "// the scheduler picks."
475..477 Comment "//"
478..553 Comment "// The desk draws its bit, then forks the seat and keeps the other end. The"
554..626 Comment "// seat draws and sends its bit, receives the desk\'s bit, then sends its"
627..702 Comment "// answer. The desk receives first and sends its bit after. The corpus runs"
703..777 Comment "// `exchanged` once for each of the four sequences of answers, and the two"
778..810 Comment "// seats always give one answer."
811..813 Comment "//"
814..887 Comment "// - see: `model/probability/draws.gandr` — the exact model at the root"
888..964 Comment "// - see: `model/probability/leader.gandr` — the exact model across worlds"
965..1034 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-dispatcher/src/evaluate.rs` — a test runs"
1035..1087 Comment "//   `exchanged` under two orders of the ready queue"
1089..1125 Comment "// The host interface of randomness."
